From 95a465edd38b1e183434930f0317fd2a8ec477df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yumi-Lab <nicolas@yumi-lab.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 18:14:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] target/arm: do not advertise FEAT_LSE2 in user-mode on
 32-bit hosts

With FEAT_LSE2 (included in the default max model) every 16-byte aligned
LDP/STP requires single-copy 16-byte atomicity.  A 32-bit host has no
16-byte atomic primitive, so the atomicity layer falls back to a
stop-the-world exclusive step for each such access.  The function
prologue stp x29,x30,[sp,#-16]! alone makes this a storm: an execution
profile of one guest runtime boot measured about 17 million exclusive
steps, 18.6 percent of all TB entries coming back through the main loop
and a saturated jump cache.

Clear ID_AA64MMFR2.AT during realize for TCG user-mode when the host is
32-bit, so the guest sees no HWCAP_USCAT and uses pre-8.4 pairwise
atomic semantics, which the LDRD/STRD fast path honours natively.  The
guest runtime boot drops from 106 s to 12 s on the reference board, with
the torn64, simd-dup2 and smc-alias batteries green.  Setting
QEMU_KEEP_LSE2=1 restores the previous behaviour, measured at 106 s
unchanged, for comparison.
---
 target/arm/cpu.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/arm/cpu.c b/target/arm/cpu.c
index da1c46e..b91bf1b 100644
--- a/target/arm/cpu.c
+++ b/target/arm/cpu.c
@@ -1985,6 +1985,24 @@ static void arm_cpu_realizefn(DeviceState *dev, Error **errp)
     tcg_cflags_set(cs, CF_PCREL);
 #endif
 
+#if defined(CONFIG_TCG) && defined(CONFIG_USER_ONLY)
+    /*
+     * On a 32-bit host there is no 16-byte atomic primitive.  With
+     * FEAT_LSE2 (part of the default `max` model) every 16-byte aligned
+     * LDP/STP requires single-copy 16-byte atomicity, which the atomicity
+     * layer can only provide by a stop-the-world exclusive step: measured
+     * ~17 M such steps for one guest runtime boot, an 8x slowdown.  Do not
+     * advertise LSE2 (HWCAP_USCAT) on such hosts; guests then use the
+     * pre-8.4 pairwise-atomic semantics that LDRD/STRD honour natively.
+     * QEMU_KEEP_LSE2=1 restores the advertised feature for comparison.
+     */
+    if (sizeof(void *) == 4 && arm_feature(env, ARM_FEATURE_AARCH64) &&
+        getenv("QEMU_KEEP_LSE2") == NULL) {
+        cpu->isar.id_aa64mmfr2 =
+            FIELD_DP64(cpu->isar.id_aa64mmfr2, ID_AA64MMFR2, AT, 0);
+    }
+#endif
+
     /* If we needed to query the host kernel for the CPU features
      * then it's possible that might have failed in the initfn, but
      * this is the first point where we can report it.
-- 
